%S A400287 1,4,28,240,1188,8352,298944,1512432,2124288,15101952,54424224,
%T A400287 386995968,839057544,1959132096,3865509888,4386628528,6683778516,
%U A400287 357047100576,684151276476,2379683794812,3053313502468,3566810670648,5009651269632,7493834581060,7551626977452
%N A400287 Numbers k such that k+1 divides phi(k)^2 + 1 where phi is Euler's totient function (A000010).
%C A400287 All prime factors of k+1 are 2 or congruent to 1 (mod 4), since -1 must be a square mod k+1; also 4 does not divide k+1. Hence every term > 1 is divisible by 4.
%C A400287 If u = 2^a*3^b with a, b >= 1, then u == 8 (mod 10) if and only if b == a+1 (mod 4).
%C A400287 Family: given such u, if q = (u+2)/10 is a prime > 3, then k = u*q is a term (equivalently, k+1 = (u^2+2u+10)/10).
%C A400287 Terms not in this family (checked up to 10^10): 1, 4, 28, 839057544 = 2^3*3^2*13*113*7933, 4386628528 = 2^4*53*443*11677, 6683778516 = 2^2*3*83*6710621.
%C A400287 The case u = 2^a (b=0, phi(u) = u/2) gives no terms, since the analogous q = (u+2)/5 is always even.
%C A400287 Of the 11 terms k <= 10^8, exactly 6 have k+1 prime: k+1 = 2, 5, 29, 241, 8353, 2124289. For these (excluding the trivial k=1 case), the condition becomes phi(p-1)^2 == -1 (mod p), equivalently A046144(p)^2 == -1 (mod p). This requires p == 1 (mod 4), a classical necessary condition for -1 to be a quadratic residue mod p. The 3 known larger sporadic terms all have k+1 composite.
%C A400287 The only prime power in this sequence is k = 4 = 2^2.
%C A400287 It is not known whether the sequence is infinite. The family would give infinitely many terms if there are infinitely many primes of the form (2^a*3^b+2)/10 with b == a+1 (mod 4).
%C A400287 a(18), if it exists, exceeds 10^10.
%e A400287 a(2) = 4: phi(4) = 2, 2^2 + 1 = 5 = 1*(4+1).
%e A400287 a(3) = 28: phi(28) = 12, 12^2 + 1 = 145 = 5*29.
%e A400287 a(4) = 240: u=48, k = 48*50/10 = 240, k+1 = (48^2+2*48+10)/10 = 241 (prime).
%o A400287 (PARI) isok(k) = Mod(eulerphi(k), k+1)^2 == -1;
%Y A400287 Cf. A000010, A046144.
%K A400287 nonn,new
%O A400287 1,2
